uestion/id #uuid "6ac0fc10-69b8-518b-a3f6-edf675029517" :question/math-academy-id "q-130153" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+11y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+11{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+11) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+11=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe auxiliary equation has pure imaginary roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+11 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-11 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm \\sqrt{11}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{11}x)+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{11}x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130153/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bf8bb23-741b-5583-b51c-67eabae0ab54"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130153"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-7816"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+16y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+16{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+16) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+16=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe auxiliary equation has pure imaginary roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-16 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-130164/selection/795c7f1650b7d8f6a93f4b8c55dae98541a7964d98c9b3708bb35a7783e1f20c" :answer/id #uuid "10d9b684-aecd-5b01-8fd5-f073aa4ae118" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pm 10\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130164/selection/2098a43979cb99eb608674685d5a81770e413a4d8d470a33599c6cac4e71c90a" :answer/id #uuid "59202476-aad7-5329-b9d6-857e81f4d37c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\pm 10\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130164/selection/7c36e0df4d9735de601a2b2eda6874a850d1bbd8fe8ff68a792b7d508ca8df78" :answer/id #uuid "40c42624-fab1-5b4e-a631-94f250b947c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130164/selection/20cb422a6fc99ed736c898598d6ff58f588a608928463f3a4ac8b1a942b8fb0f" :answer/id #uuid "b7c9beba-e160-59c4-b7e4-6c07ddb3ef68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 10\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130164/selection/d02b475d97a113aedf2376efcb256070c09e7c27515b4ccf3c96ecc7aff0053a" :answer/id #uuid "cae6e323-3422-5ca6-82c6-95937d9871a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10\\pm 3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130164/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9a525e3-4dce-5179-ae10-9657f31b095c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130164/selection/2098a43979cb99eb608674685d5a81770e413a4d8d470a33599c6cac4e71c90a" :answer-field/choices ["q-130164/selection/795c7f1650b7d8f6a93f4b8c55dae98541a7964d98c9b3708bb35a7783e1f20c" "q-130164/selection/2098a43979cb99eb608674685d5a81770e413a4d8d470a33599c6cac4e71c90a" "q-130164/selection/7c36e0df4d9735de601a2b2eda6874a850d1bbd8fe8ff68a792b7d508ca8df78" "q-130164/selection/20cb422a6fc99ed736c898598d6ff58f588a608928463f3a4ac8b1a942b8fb0f" "q-130164/selection/d02b475d97a113aedf2376efcb256070c09e7c27515b4ccf3c96ecc7aff0053a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130164" :question/id #uuid "97069a00-838c-503e-8cc1-9576f402268b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130164" :question/problem "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+109y=0,$ where $y=y(x).$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ is a solution, then $\\lambda =$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+6\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+109{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +109) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +109=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +109 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +9)-9+109 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2}+100 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2} & =-100 \\\\ \\lambda +3 & =\\pm 10\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-3\\pm 10\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $\\lambda =-3\\pm 10\\text{i}$ are the complex roots of the auxiliary equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130164/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "191e98e0-aa31-5dd9-a735-6580d29ad287"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130164"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64663"] :question/problem "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}-6{y}^{′}+10y=0$ where $y=y(t).$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ is a solution, then $\\lambda =$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}-6\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t}+10{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +10) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +10=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +10 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +9)-9+10 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda -3 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =3\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $\\lambda =3\\pm \\text{i}$ are the complex roots of the auxiliary equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-90797/selection/497113acdb2e9b54272b6cc8ca3f924faeb232e49ef4548dd5e3c9800f23dbd3" :answer/id #uuid "707b4973-a4d4-5d05-8a5f-1dcad90207eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90797/selection/57575d0311a2ec2f497eae31b1d0638f2e1047d51ea4ccc82384abed493fe69b" :answer/id #uuid "cbdd4a44-5838-5c87-9f85-7339e4156bea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pm 4\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90797/selection/55600de523933f0f30f1e959326f390c0977566aa0af9035f33094e1d8ce2782" :answer/id #uuid "78337f75-a73a-5716-a9b7-e31ea8a2ec9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90797/selection/9d1548e17123cd2ea0a7b39699e279cafdc784ae0892266ea789503ea99f4f8a" :answer/id #uuid "376ae6c9-3f82-5515-ab04-08c3848be71c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 4\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90797/selection/9111b7927ef7176668675d518b5dbddd5775d87ba956d01cf762504c03151dea" :answer/id #uuid "98a6dc2e-c80a-5c9d-a959-dff81a39d659" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\pm 2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90797/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3df23489-71b4-5ad0-b9f7-9d102efe8254" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90797/selection/9111b7927ef7176668675d518b5dbddd5775d87ba956d01cf762504c03151dea" :answer-field/choices ["q-90797/selection/497113acdb2e9b54272b6cc8ca3f924faeb232e49ef4548dd5e3c9800f23dbd3" "q-90797/selection/57575d0311a2ec2f497eae31b1d0638f2e1047d51ea4ccc82384abed493fe69b" "q-90797/selection/55600de523933f0f30f1e959326f390c0977566aa0af9035f33094e1d8ce2782" "q-90797/selection/9d1548e17123cd2ea0a7b39699e279cafdc784ae0892266ea789503ea99f4f8a" "q-90797/selection/9111b7927ef7176668675d518b5dbddd5775d87ba956d01cf762504c03151dea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90797" :question/id #uuid "aa6c5a43-700b-58fe-9c09-aaa67bfd669a" :question/math-academy-id "q-90797" :question/problem "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+8y=0,$ where $y=y(x).$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ is a solution, then $\\lambda =$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+4\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+8{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +8=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4)-4+8 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda +2 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-2\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $\\lambda =-2\\pm 2\\text{i}$ are the complex roots of the auxiliary equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-90797/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "191e98e0-aa31-5dd9-a735-6580d29ad287"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90797"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64694"] :question/problem "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}+12{y}^{′}+40y=0,$ where $y=y(x).$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ is a solution, then $\\lambda =$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+12\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+40{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+12\\lambda +40) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+12\\lambda +40=0\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+12\\lambda +40 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+12\\lambda +36)-36+40 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +6)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +6)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda +6 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-6\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $\\lambda =-6\\pm 2\\text{i}$ are the complex roots of the auxiliary equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-90799/selection/91d0eb84e8e207218a94ade0446638226848d721b56eedad6de61671a823d9fd" :answer/id #uuid "f43e1fcd-e457-5dcb-b57e-95e0864