quation ${y}^{″}+3y=0,$ where $y=y(t).$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ is a solution, then $\\lambda =$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}+3{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}+3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+3=0.\n$$\n\nSolving the auxiliary equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+3 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-3 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $\\lambda =\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}$ are the (purely imaginary) roots of the auxiliary equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-90799/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "191e98e0-aa31-5dd9-a735-6580d29ad287"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90799"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90802/selection/fedd4f31914a12f1d70936632684e042a01f0e9a5fbb0049294da32a6cbb4988" :answer/id #uuid "b3561c27-7095-5ce9-9abf-bf1ff12419ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90802/selection/942374a1a9f911509fdc336dac55b33be65a9ec5ea8cf1acddfa8939e84fa1e5" :answer/id #uuid "1e76a656-4872-5eb7-a62f-eb218492341f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{4x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90802/selection/e77d0c2a6559bf3cea6ce7863938140a071d095f10721299f115644b7e63fe39" :answer/id #uuid "fe3bbc81-1fb1-5ed1-a927-44c9967b450e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90802/selection/6acdfc30b96396abdde11328800c318d1b01d55e256d6adaced278dfdc06ddc2" :answer/id #uuid "b2ddddc7-b901-51ad-b54a-d33ae87d3e26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90802/selection/ac101600d4bd90db9d4b0557d75a9a57d51e583a8d32c91ff63dcd67c9700fc2" :answer/id #uuid "d99076a4-14eb-5ece-99d3-91290f3d87df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-4x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90802/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "430f270b-181a-50bd-8766-9d93fae3e7b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90802/selection/6acdfc30b96396abdde11328800c318d1b01d55e256d6adaced278dfdc06ddc2" :answer-field/choices ["q-90802/selection/fedd4f31914a12f1d70936632684e042a01f0e9a5fbb0049294da32a6cbb4988" "q-90802/selection/942374a1a9f911509fdc336dac55b33be65a9ec5ea8cf1acddfa8939e84fa1e5" "q-90802/selection/e77d0c2a6559bf3cea6ce7863938140a071d095f10721299f115644b7e63fe39" "q-90802/selection/6acdfc30b96396abdde11328800c318d1b01d55e256d6adaced278dfdc06ddc2" "q-90802/selection/ac101600d4bd90db9d4b0557d75a9a57d51e583a8d32c91ff63dcd67c9700fc2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90802" :question/id #uuid "9ee9204f-cbf7-5f8e-aa10-c66f362b4cd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-90802" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+8y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-4\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+8{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +8=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4)-4+8 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda -2 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =2\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-90802/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2999a565-bf64-5246-9fee-54cecc9e79ff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90802"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-7818"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+26y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+26{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +26) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +26=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +26 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1)-1+26 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2} & =-25 \\\\ \\lambda +1 & =\\pm 5\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-1\\pm 5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-130327/selection/17dff2c0f99ff386d20fb3f386c99a8ab44e4f72b142bb710ecc716229c510ef" :answer/id #uuid "60a816ee-349d-5d90-ae4f-bab8437d14ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{10x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130327/selection/9fc5a397354305fbed77bd6f01fdfec67654b3c7d51862948bd72dd6558a947d" :answer/id #uuid "0932d06b-ddf6-5a06-84f6-0d97052f23ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-3x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130327/selection/ba431090a93b487550fbf3e1dce658d5ddb3be80fdccb0bf615b310c4ebcc5c9" :answer/id #uuid "b1f3648e-ccc1-5411-bd6b-f2dd691fb6c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{3x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130327/selection/3f6d26964345dad877fc9042d2285dce6df3c09d2e5e3c0e4386df0f78fcd3f9" :answer/id #uuid "80b22cca-2551-5598-8ee8-02c08c8f76de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{10x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130327/selection/a47fe61d5d60a5fd621d23635e5db8a2a45b26ea267a4ea3ae28e05a5e5da89a" :answer/id #uuid "e76a883f-0f76-50c5-b03d-9b9415908410" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-10x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130327/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "73ec17ea-3870-591f-af0d-a3c990fe2231" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130327/selection/9fc5a397354305fbed77bd6f01fdfec67654b3c7d51862948bd72dd6